{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Input Sphere module provides a visual and interactive way to control a robot’s end effector in 3D space using visionOS."}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/robokit\/inputsphere"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/InputSphere"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Input Sphere module creates a virtual sphere that can be positioned and rotated in 3D space to represent the desired pose (position and orientation) of a robot’s end effector. This module provides coordinate transformations between visionOS (RealityKit) and ROS (Robot Operating System) coordinate systems, making it easy to integrate with robotic applications."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Setup","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Setup"},{"level":3,"text":"Initialize Input Sphere Manager","type":"heading","anchor":"Initialize-Input-Sphere-Manager"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Create an instance of the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/InputSphereManager","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to track and update the position and orientation of the Input Sphere:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import RoboKit","","@State private var inputSphereManager = InputSphereManager()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Add-Input-Sphere-to-RealityKit-Scene","type":"heading","text":"Add Input Sphere to RealityKit Scene"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the Input Sphere to your RealityKit scene with the appropriate parent and rootPoint entities:"}]},{"code":[".onAppear {","    inputSphereManager.addInputSphere(parentEntity: parentEntity, rootPoint: rootPoint)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Usage","text":"Usage","type":"heading"},{"text":"Control Input Sphere Position","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Control-Input-Sphere-Position"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Update the position of the Input Sphere using a drag gesture:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Add Input Sphere Drag Gesture recognition and handling.",".inputSphereDragGesture(","    parentEntity: parentEntity,","    rootPoint: rootPoint,","    inputSphereManager: inputSphereManager",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","text":"Control Input Sphere Orientation","level":3,"anchor":"Control-Input-Sphere-Orientation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Update the orientation of the Input Sphere using Euler angles:"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Set orientation using roll, pitch, and yaw","inputSphereManager.inputSphereEulerAngles = [","    .roll: Float.pi \/ 4,   \/\/ 45 degrees","    .yaw: 0,","    .pitch: Float.pi \/ 6   \/\/ 30 degrees","]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Track-Input-Sphere-Position","level":3,"text":"Track Input Sphere Position","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Monitor the position of the Input Sphere relative to a root point in your scene:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ Get position in ROS coordinate system","if let position = inputSphereManager.getInputSpherePosition(relativeToRootPoint: rootEntity) {","    print(\"Input Sphere position (ROS): \\(position)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","text":"Track Input Sphere Orientation","level":3,"anchor":"Track-Input-Sphere-Orientation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Monitor the orientation of the Input Sphere relative to a root point in your scene:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ Get position in ROS coordinate system","if let orientation = inputSphereManager.getInputSphereRotation(relativeToRootPoint: rootEntity) {","    print(\"Input Sphere orientation (ROS): \\(orientation)\")","}"]},{"anchor":"Display-Input-Sphere-Data","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Display Input Sphere Data"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/InputSpherePositionView"},{"type":"text","text":" to your SwiftUI interface to display the current position:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["InputSpherePositionView(relativeToRootPoint: rootEntity)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Enable-Interactive-Control","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Enable Interactive Control"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Allow users to adjust the Input Sphere using the rotation sliders:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["VStack {","    InputSphereRotationSlider(eulerAngle: .roll)","    InputSphereRotationSlider(eulerAngle: .pitch)","    InputSphereRotationSlider(eulerAngle: .yaw)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"style":"important","type":"aside","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Remember that the Input Sphere uses different coordinate systems for RealityKit and ROS. Position and rotation values are automatically converted when using the appropriate getter methods.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","images":[{"identifier":"InputSphereCard.png","type":"card"}],"modules":[{"name":"RoboKit"}],"role":"article","title":"Input Sphere"},"references":{"doc://robokit.RoboKit/documentation/RoboKit":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/robokit","title":"RoboKit","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"RoboKitLogo.png"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"RoboKit is a framework designed to facilitate the integration between visionOS applications and robotics software."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit"},"doc://robokit.RoboKit/documentation/RoboKit/InputSphereManager":{"title":"InputSphereManager","identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/InputSphereManager","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InputSphereManager","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"InputSphereManager","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/robokit\/inputspheremanager","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A class responsible for managing the Input Sphere, which represents the desired position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and orientation of a robot’s end effector in a 3D environment."}]},"RoboKitLogo.png":{"type":"image","alt":"RoboKit logo.","identifier":"RoboKitLogo.png","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/robokit.RoboKit\/RoboKitLogo.png","traits":["1x","light"]},{"traits":["1x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/robokit.RoboKit\/RoboKitLogo~dark.png"}]},"doc://robokit.RoboKit/documentation/RoboKit/InputSpherePositionView":{"title":"InputSpherePositionView","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"InputSpherePositionView"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"InputSpherePositionView","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/robokit.RoboKit\/documentation\/RoboKit\/InputSpherePositionView","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A SwiftUI view that displays the position of the Input Sphere relative to a specified root point.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/robokit\/inputspherepositionview"},"InputSphereCard.png":{"type":"image","alt":null,"identifier":"InputSphereCard.png","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/robokit.RoboKit\/InputSphereCard.png","traits":["1x","light"]}]}}}